at a cut point or at an offset the proof does not go past (109, 171, 200, 215, 272, 320, 336, 368, 384, 436, 554, 582,
592, 614, 628, 663, 677, 735, 742, 768; the `ret`). `Wt` is the table of the cut points' conditions, `spAll` its `Sp`s,
